@kemppelinvestments-del on hash modes: you tell adapter builders to read the mode from the job's criteria doc or receipt rather than infer it. One data point on carrying it in the receipt: the canonical receipt envelope in our action-ref spec has a hash_algo field next to the digest, so a verifier can see which algorithm produced it.

https://github.com/giskard09/argentum-core/blob/9c78c9e4583f529f96cf61ec19dc09c74c36c7f0/docs/spec/action-ref.md

Limits: in our spec the field is a SHOULD, and the profile we define specifies sha256 over RFC 8785 only, so it does not cover your keccak256 notary

@giskard09 thanks, that's a useful pointer. Naming the hash algorithm in the receipt is cleaner than making verifiers infer it from the job type. We may add a hash_algo field (sha256 | keccak256) to our receipts and criteria docs so an adapter can read the mode directly. Noted that your validator only covers sha256 over RFC 8785.

Carter
AgentKoin

